+# Korean (한국어) interface
+
+ArtCraft Launcher can be shown in Korean. **Settings → Language → Korean** picks it; **Auto** picks
+it when the system's preferred language is Korean (`ko`, `ko-KR`, `ko_KR.UTF-8`, `ko-KP`,
+`ko-Kore-KR`…; on Windows that is the display language, which a Korean PC reports as `ko-KR`).
+`ARTCRAFT_LAUNCHER_LOCALE=ko` tries it without changing the setting.
+
+## Provenance
+
+The catalog (`crates/ui-egui/src/i18n/ko.tsv`), the per-script system font support and the Korean
+tests are based on **storytold/craft-launcher#285, "Add Korean localization and system font
+support", by back2zion** (open, unmerged at the time of the port). Only the Korean parts of that
+pull request were taken into v0.3.2:
+
+| Taken from #285 | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `ko.tsv` | the translation itself |
+| `Script` in the language registry (replacing the `cjk` flag), `cjk_font::load(script)` and the Korean font candidates | Korean needs a Hangul face; the Chinese faces (Microsoft YaHei, SimSun, PingFang SC…) have none, so one shared "CJK font" can't serve both |
+| A font cache per language in `theme.rs`; `install_fonts(ctx, Option<Lang>)`; `cjk_font_available/loaded(lang)` | the face loaded must be the one for the language shown |
+| `Settings::language_label(code, installed)` | the picker may only write "한국어" while the Korean face is the one installed; with the Chinese face loaded it would be drawn as boxes |
+| The Korean unit tests and `tests/korean.rs` | adapted to the revised rows below |
+
+Left out, as not needed for Korean: the Czech, Spanish, Polish, Hungarian and Japanese catalogs,
+the app details page, hidden apps, motion settings, logging, packaging and CI changes, and the
+baseline nudge for fallback faces (`face_metrics`). The latter changes how Chinese renders too;
+see Limits.
+
+Of the 287 rows in v0.3.2's Korean catalog:
+
+- **261** are back2zion's rows as written in #285;
+- **25** are revised (table below);
+- **1** is new: `Classic` → `클래식`, a row the reference catalogs (pt-BR, zh-CN) carry;
+- 19 rows of #285 were dropped because they translate features v0.3.2 doesn't have (app details,
+  pictures, hidden apps).
+
+The revisions and the new row were made with AI assistance (Claude) and **have not been reviewed by
+a native Korean speaker**. Corrections are welcome.
+
+### Revised rows
+
+| Context | English | #285 | Now | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| | Open | 열기 | 실행 | the button launches the app; 실행 is the launcher term |
+| `@id` | app.open | 열기 | 실행 | same |
+| | Open ArtCraft Launcher to update. | …를 열어… | ArtCraft Launcher를 실행하여 업데이트하세요. | same |
+| | Classic apps | 기존 앱 | 클래식 앱 | 기존 reads as "existing/old" |
+| | Inspired by | 참고 앱 | 유사 제품 | the sort key is the known product an app resembles |
+| `@id` | sort.inspired | 참고 앱 | 유사 제품 | same |
+| | Appearance | 화면 설정 | 모양 | Photoshop (인터페이스 > 모양) and Windows term |
+| `@id` | appearance.theme | 화면 설정 | 모양 | same |
+| | Show in Explorer | 탐색기에서 보기 | 파일 탐색기에서 보기 | Windows' own name |
+| | Only when I ask | 직접 요청할 때만 | 수동 | short menu item, pairs with 자동 |
+| | Tarball (.tar.gz) | 압축 파일(.tar.gz) | tar 압축 파일(.tar.gz) | keep the technology name |
+| `column` | Installed | 설치됨 | 설치된 버전 | the column shows a version |
+| `column` | Latest | 최신 | 최신 버전 | same |
+| | Download / Install / Update / Uninstall cancelled (4 rows) | … 취소됨 | …를 취소했습니다. | toast messages in 합니다체 |
+| `@msg` | Download cancelled | 다운로드 취소됨 | 다운로드를 취소했습니다. | same |
+| both | Couldn't open {name}: {e} (2 rows) | {name} 열기 실패: {e} | {name} 앱을 열 수 없습니다: {e} | message in 합니다체 |
+| `@msg` | {name} updated to {version} (and its no-checksum form) | {name} 업데이트 완료: {version}… | {name} 앱을 {version} 버전으로 업데이트했습니다.… | same |
+| `@msg` | {name} installed: {version} (and its no-checksum form) | {name} 설치 완료: {version}… | {name} {version} 버전을 설치했습니다.… | same |
+| `@msg` | {name} was removed | {name} 제거 완료 | {name} 앱을 제거했습니다. | same |
+
+## Style and terminology
+
+- Menus, buttons, filters and column headers are short nouns (설치, 업데이트, 실행, 제거).
+  Messages, notices and tooltips are full sentences in 합니다체 (…했습니다, …하세요).
+- Placeholders (`{name}`, `{version}`, `{n}`…), units, file formats (`.msi`, `.dmg`, `.tar.gz`,
+  RAW, PDF), technology and platform names (Flatpak, RPM, Debian, GitHub, Discord, Finder,
+  Windows, macOS, Linux) and every product name (ArtCraft Launcher, Craft App Suite, PhotoCraft…)
+  stay in English.
+- `{name}` is followed by 앱 (`{name} 앱을…`) so no 을/를 particle has to agree with an English name.
+- Korean has one plural form: `앱 {n}개`, `{n}분 전`, `{n}일 전`.
+
+| English | Korean | Note |
+|---|---|---|
+| App | 앱 | |
+| Install / Installing… | 설치 / 설치 중… | |
+| Update / Update available | 업데이트 / 업데이트 가능 | |
+| Open (launch) | 실행 | |
+| Uninstall / Remove | 제거 | |
+| Download | 다운로드 | |
+| Settings | 설정 | |
+| Library (photo library) | 라이브러리 | Lightroom term |
+| New version | 새 버전 | |
+| Release notes | 릴리스 노트 | |
+| What's new | 새로운 기능 | Adobe term |
+| Release / Released | 릴리스 / 출시일 | |
+| Pre-releases | 시험판 | |
+| Checksum | 체크섬 | |
+| Appearance | 모양 | Photoshop, Windows |
+| Restore (window) | 이전 크기로 | Windows |
+| Trash | 휴지통 | |
+| File Explorer | 파일 탐색기 | Windows |
+| Grid / Table view | 격자 / 표 | 격자 보기 as in Lightroom |
+| Portable | 포터블 | |
+| Raw development | RAW 현상 | Lightroom term |
+
+## Fonts
+
+No font is bundled (AGENTS.md: never bundle a CJK font). Korean is drawn with a Hangul face the
+system already has, appended behind the bundled Latin faces in every UI family, so Latin text,
+digits and punctuation keep Inter, Archivo and Geist Mono and Hangul falls through to the system
+face. The face is looked for only when Korean is chosen (or Auto resolves to it), in this order:
+
+| System | Faces, best first |
+|---|---|
+| Windows | **Malgun Gothic** (`%SystemRoot%\Fonts\malgun.ttf`, its Regular face), then Gulim (`gulim.ttc`) |
+| macOS | Apple SD Gothic Neo (`/System/Library/Fonts/AppleSDGothicNeo.ttc`, or the downloaded font asset), then AppleGothic |
+| Linux, FreeBSD | Noto Sans CJK KR (`NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc`, `NotoSansCJKkr-Regular.otf`, `NotoSansCJK-VF.ttc`), Noto Sans KR, NanumGothic |
+
+On a Korean Windows PC that is Malgun Gothic Regular (it ships with every Windows since Vista).
+If none is found, the interface stays in English and Settings says so (in English, since Korean
+can't be drawn), rather than drawing boxes. The web build has no system fonts, so Korean stays in
+English there.
+
+## Tests
+
+- `crates/ui-egui/src/i18n/tests.rs`: locale tags (`korean_locales_resolve`), counts, dates,
+  terminology and 합니다체 messages (`korean_counts_dates_and_messages_work`), parity with every
+  other catalog (`korean_catalog_has_every_row_of_the_other_catalogs`), no Han or kana in the
+  catalog (`korean_catalog_uses_no_han_or_kana`), the picker labels
+  (`language_labels_come_from_the_registry`), and glyph coverage in every UI family
+  (`system_font_covers_korean_in_every_ui_family`, skipped with a message without a Korean font).
+  The shared catalog tests (format, placeholders, plural forms, `…`, coverage of every `tl!`
+  literal, taglines, package formats) run on `ko.tsv` too.
+- `crates/ui-egui/src/cjk_font.rs`: `korean_face_covers_the_catalogs_hangul` checks every Hangul
+  character in `ko.tsv` against the Korean face's character map. It uses the system face, or the
+  file in `ARTCRAFT_LAUNCHER_TEST_KOREAN_FONT` (any face in it with Hangul) on machines without
+  one, and skips with a message otherwise. `windows_draws_korean_with_malgun_gothic` (Windows
+  only) pins the candidate order.
+- `crates/ui-egui/tests/korean.rs`: picks Korean in Settings, checks it persists, the main views
+  and the install actions (or the English fallback and its note without a Korean font).
+
+```sh
+cargo test -p artcraft-launcher-ui-egui --lib korean
+cargo test -p artcraft-launcher-ui-egui --lib i18n
+ARTCRAFT_LAUNCHER_TEST_KOREAN_FONT=/path/to/NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc \
+  cargo test -p artcraft-launcher-ui-egui --lib korean_face_covers -- --nocapture
+cargo test -p artcraft-launcher-ui-egui --test korean
+```
+
+## Limits
+
+- Not reviewed by a native speaker (see Provenance).
+- Hangul is drawn at the system face's Regular weight in every family, including the bold and
+  display ones; Malgun Gothic Bold isn't loaded.
+- Fallback faces sit on their own ascent in egui, so Hangul can ride slightly off the Latin
+  baseline; #285's `face_metrics` nudge wasn't ported because it changes Chinese rendering too.
+- Search matches the English app names, taglines and "like" names only: a Hangul query
+  (`이미지`) finds nothing.
+- Release notes and other text from GitHub are shown as published.
+- Korean text entry: the search box is an egui `TextEdit`, which handles IME composition
+  (`Event::Ime` `Preedit`/`Commit`) itself, and eframe/egui-winit turn winit's IME events into
+  those and enable the IME while a text field has focus; the launcher adds nothing on top. Not
+  checked by hand with the Windows Korean IME.
